――New questions sprouted, new challenges were set, and just as they resolved to get things moving, circumstances, as they often do, refused to progress according to plan.

More often than not, the path to achieving a goal is obstructed by stagnation in the environment or, conversely, by unexpected upheaval. In this case, it was the latter that had thwarted Natsuki Subaru just as he was getting started.

"――*faa*..."

A soft breath escaped as a hand was brought to a mouth just beginning to open wide, hiding the yawn.

However, it was an obviously visible yawn, and they could even see the tear droplets welling up in the other person's eyes. It made Subaru wonder, as he often did, which was considered more polite by etiquette standards: yawning openly, or stifling a yawn only to have tears well up? If one were to say that simply yawning at all was a breach of manners, then there was nothing more to discuss.

"――It's just some rough tea, but please."

As he watched the other person while pondering such things, a cup of black tea, brewed by Petra showcasing the tea-pouring techniques she had learned from Ram, was gently placed on the table.

As the warm, aromatic fragrance of the high-quality leaves wafted over, "Oh my," the other person's yawn was interrupted.

"What a lovely aroma. Even though I've dropped by so suddenly like this, to be treated so hospitably... it almost makes me feel a bit awkward, hehe."

"Oh no, it's fine. We were just about to have tea ourselves, so actually, I think your timing was perfect. Um..."

"――It's Sakura Element, Emilia-chan."

Saying this, the woman with a faint smile – Sakura Element, a member of the 'Dragon God Church' – brought the offered teacup to her lips without hesitation.

Sakura had arrived at the Royal Palace Guest House where the Emilia camp was staying around the time between early morning and breakfast, when Subaru and the others were just starting to feel their minds wake up. Coming from Subaru and the others, it wasn't their place to say, but an unannounced visit like this felt somewhat like a surprise attack...

"We would have liked to extend our greetings as well, but Emilia-sama is a very busy person with many things she needs to attend to. Ideally, we would have appreciated prior contact."

His rhythm thrown off by the other party, Otto seemed rather displeased. Although his choice of words was polite, the hint of protest was clearly palpable in Otto's statement, and Subaru thought he seemed quite on edge.

"Guess the venting yesterday wasn't enough... He seems to think that as long as he uses polite language, he's being courteous to the other person."

"I *can* hear you, you know. This is troubling, Natsuki-san."

"Whoa, that's not courtesy, that's a threat..."

Despite being an ally, Otto snapped back mercilessly, but his battle-ready state was, of course, not about punishing Subaru and the others but because they were hosting a person requiring utmost caution. Coming right on the heels of yesterday's events, no one would fail to connect the 'Dragon God Church,' currently the center of attention, deliberately showing up at their place with the Royal Selection.

Naturally, Sakura, whom they had shown into the reception room, was also considered to have a reason to be wary of – but...

"――You're Subaru-chan, right? Staring so intently like that makes me blush, you know."

"Ah, sorry. Sakura-san is beautiful, was I being rude?"

"My, apologizing while flirting, what a naughty boy. I didn't think you were so smooth. I've heard various rumors about you, Subaru-chan."

"Rumors? About me?"

At the unexpected counter, Subaru pointed to himself, and Sakura smiled, saying "Yes." She then stirred her tea with a teaspoon, brought the cup to her lips again, and let out a sigh with a somehow alluring gesture.

Afterwards, tilting her head at the vague silence that had emerged,

"...Could it be, was I supposed to say something just now?"

"Well, following that conversation, wouldn't you expect me to wonder what rumors about me Sakura-san has heard?"

"Hmm? But wouldn't Emilia-chan and the others from your own camp know much more about Subaru-chan than I do? What kind of rumors are circulating about Subaru-chan now... isn't that kind of irrelevant?"

"I see, you make a good point, perhaps. Indeed, Betty and the others know Subaru best. There's no need to worry about anything, is there?"

"That's right. Having such a splendid knight makes me very proud too."

Having Beatrice on her lap and Emilia to his right vouch for him so strongly, Subaru was happy but also felt oddly unsatisfied as the rumor topic was brushed aside.

Anyway, including Petra standing by the wall, the current situation was Subaru, Emilia, Beatrice, and Otto receiving Sakura, who had launched this unannounced assault.

Currently, Sakura's impression was that of a woman whose intentions were difficult to grasp, but...

"Sakura-san, are you close with Filioare? I only just became friends with her."

"Yes, Filioare-chan has told me about you so much it's almost tiresome. She goes on and on about 'my Emilia' this and 'my Emilia' that... Well, I suppose I'm something like a colleague of Filioare-chan's at the church, and also a sort of older sister figure to her."

"Filioare's big sister!"

"Wow, quite a difference in energy between those sisters, huh?"

"It's only 'like' an older sister, you know. That child was raised hidden away, cherished dearly as the church's treasure, so you could also say she's like the youngest daughter of the entire church. Ufufu."

Sakura's smile, as she spoke with softened eyes, maintained a constant warmth. So how much of her explanation about Filioare could be taken seriously was a mystery.

However, the description of Filioare as the church's treasured, hidden child was intriguing.

"So, are we to understand that Filioare-san not appearing on the public stage until now was due to the policy of the 'Dragon God Church'?"

"Yes, that's right. Well, that policy became meaningless because Filioare-chan herself went and burst out onto the scene, though."

"So Filioare's runaway was genuinely unexpected by the church, huh..."

If you didn't know the person, you wouldn't believe it no matter what, but having actually spoken with Filioare, Subaru found this development not at all strange. Just yesterday, she had been forcibly ordered to stay in the church, but judging by her demeanor, it seemed like she'd reach her limit of patience quickly and burst out on her own.

"In fact, she did burst out. And that's why I'm here visiting Emilia-chan and everyone today."

"...Eh!? She burst out? You mean today!?"

"Yes, this morning. I'd thoroughly instructed her about today's plans yesterday, but she's such a troublesome girl..."

"Wait, wait, wait, is this really the time to be calmly sipping tea calling her troublesome!?"

Although not officially announced, there was no doubt Filioare had rapidly ascended to the status of an important figure in the kingdom. For her to be acting on her own while her chaperone was relaxing here – that didn't seem right.

As Subaru and the others panicked, Sakura laughed "Ufufu" as if it didn't concern her.

"You can rest assured there. You see, we know exactly where Filioare-chan was headed. Straight to her friend Emilia-chan's place."

"Ah, I see, so that's it. To my place... she's not here!?"

"She's not here, right!?"

Just when they thought it might be reassuring, the information failed to be, and the panic continued.

Given Sakura's confident tone, there might have been a note from Filioare stating her destination, but none of the camp members had seen hide nor hair of the girl herself. Of course, Petra and Otto also didn't know her whereabouts.

"Beako doesn't know either, of course. She's been with me all day since waking up."

"Indeed. Woke up early with Subaru, brushed teeth with Subaru, did radio exercises with Subaru, then had breakfast with Subaru. Betty hasn't seen that noisy girl during that time either."

"Wh-what should we do? If something's happened to Filioare..."

Exchanging looks, Subaru and the others were deeply troubled by the whereabouts of the vanished Filioare. When she suddenly appeared, they were shocked by her existence, and now learning she had suddenly disappeared brought a different kind of shock. Filioare was like a human-shaped storm.

Then, amidst their flustered state, Otto let out a small sigh beside them.

"Hey, what's up, Otto... Oh! Don't tell me you're thinking it'd be less troublesome if she just disappeared altogether..."

"Otto, that would be going a bit too far, even for Roswaal, wouldn't it..."

"Please stop with the reputational damage. Beatrice-chan, don't look at me like that either... Just to confirm, was Filioare-san wearing the nun's habit of the 'Dragon God Church'?"

With a vein bulging at the looks from the embracing Subaru and Beatrice, Otto then asked Sakura about Filioare's attire. When Sakura nodded, saying "Of course,"

"Then there's no need to worry. Unless something extraordinary happens, a woman dressed as a nun of the 'Dragon God Church' won't get caught up in trouble on the streets."

"Really? Petra-chan, is that true?"

"Yes, I think Otto-san is right. If someone from the church was in trouble, I'm sure someone nearby would definitely lend a hand."

At Otto and Petra's confident, matter-of-fact statements, Subaru and Emilia felt enlightened, thinking "Is that so?"

"But that's only if she's in trouble on the streets, right? What about scenarios like, say, falling into the evil clutches of some malicious person... wouldn't that guarantee be less certain then?"

"What is this 'evil,' 'wicked,' 'malicious' someone you're talking about... Judging from Sakura-san's attitude, that worry is probably unfounded. In the first place, the reason she's here is―"

"――Otto-chan is so quick-witted, isn't he? Exactly right, I came ahead."

Just as Otto was about to state his conclusion, confident he had reached it, Sakura swooped in and voiced the reason for her own visit to the Royal Palace Guest House. Her phrasing was slightly lacking in detail, but combined with the content and the actual Filioare's headstrong nature, Subaru arrived at the answer a beat behind Otto.

"In other words, Filioare said she was going to Emilia-tan's place, but since she doesn't know the exact location, she's been asking around for directions on her way here..."

"And you, her 'like an older sister,' got here before Filioare, who'll eventually arrive, and are now calmly having tea with Betty and the others."

"Clap, clap, clap. Perfectly correct. The children at Emilia-chan's place are exceptionally capable, aren't they?"

Sakura gave a small round of applause in praise, but Subaru and the others weren't naive enough to take the compliment at face value. Besides, even combining kindness towards a member of the 'Dragon God Church' with Filioare's initiative, could they really be absolutely certain she was safe?

Emilia seemed to share the same worry, as she furrowed her beautifully shaped brows.

"Sakura-san sounds confident, but I'm worried about Filioare. Maybe I should go look around the area―"

"――Emilia-san, pardon me. You have a visitor."

Emilia's concern was interrupted just then by Rem's voice knocking on the reception room door. Instantly, everyone's gaze turned to the door, and Emilia tilted her head, asking, "A visitor?"

And then, the next moment, the door was flung open with a bang from the other side――

"――It's terrible, Emilia! Please help me, your friend!"

"Filioare!?"

Before Emilia's eyes, which widened in surprise, the one who came rushing noisily into the reception room was none other than Filioare, the very subject of their conversation. With her crimson eyes glistening, she ran towards the watching Emilia and, without slowing her momentum at all, dove headfirst into her chest. The force of it was practically a headbutt, but Emilia effortlessly caught and embraced the charging Filioare.

"Wah, you surprised me! Are you okay, Filioare? Are you hurt?"

"Yes, yes, I'm fine... No, that's not it! I'm a wreck! Look, not my body, my heart is in tatters!"

"Oh no, that's terrible... Where should I look?"

"I don't know either, so just hold me tight!"

"Okay! *Squeeze!*"

Filioare, from the moment she entered, was dyeing the space in her own color with tremendous force. Emilia's gallant nature shone through as she responded without hesitation to Filioare's impulsive words and actions.

As they watched the two embrace, Petra sidled up beside Subaru and tugged on the sleeve of his tracksuit.

"...That's the rumored 'Saint'-sama?"

"That's the rumored 'Saint'-sama. How is she? Different from your image?"

"Quite different, maybe... Ah, but I think it's fine. 'Saints' come in all types, after all!"

"The era of diverse 'Saints,' huh... doesn't really resonate with me."

Even for Petra, good at both listening and speaking, her overwhelmed state couldn't be easily put into words.

Anyway, the worst-case scenario of Filioare, wandering the royal capital alone, failing to reach the Royal Palace Guest House, had been averted for now.

"Now then, about Filioare's purpose, which she claims needs 'help'..."

"Somehow, I have a bad feeling about this."

Subaru completely agreed with Beatrice's speculation. Ignoring them, Emilia soothed Filioare, who was gradually calming down in her arms, with a gentle voice.

"So, can you tell me what happened? What do you mean by 'help'?"

"Well, you see... something terrible has happened, Emilia."

"Terrible... *gulp*"

At Filioare's suspenseful phrasing, Emilia audibly swallowed. Looking closely at Emilia, Filioare continued.

It was――

"――It seems I have to participate in the Royal Selection as a candidate!"

Filioare lamented this cruel fate imposed upon her, her voice cracking with tears.

Hearing this, Emilia's violet-blue eyes flew wide open, Otto brought a hand to his forehead, Petra bit her lip on her cute face, and Subaru and Beatrice exchanged glances.

"Just as expected..."

"Our bad feeling was right."

"What should I do... Gah! Sakura!?"

As Subaru and the others succeeded in their unpleasant prediction, Sakura, whose presence Filioare hadn't confirmed because her back was turned to the entrance, waved at her from the side.

At this unexpected encounter with her associate, Filioare, who had brought the commotion, opened her mouth so wide it seemed her jaw might drop. ――It completely ruined the beautiful girl's image.
